[sliver] Specific required legend relief: the integral disposal warning (hardware/markings/README.md: UL 60335-2-24 7.1DV.4.1(d), letters at least 6.4 mm) is raised lettering, as Derek asked: 6.5 mm Helvetica Bold caps 0.6 mm proud of back-bottom's +Y wall, which prints floor-down so every layer draws the letters as bumps in its outer wall. These strips are the letters' 0.6 mm relief flanks and the 1.35 mm faces of each I. At 6.4 mm a bold stroke is 0.96-1.41 mm; 3 mm strokes would need letters about 15 mm tall.
alternatives: The raked legend keeps these 0.6 mm flanks; 3 mm strokes would need letters about 15 mm tall.
