[thin] Specific cosmetic-flute profile exception: these short material chords belong to the retained exterior groove, fade and opening-edge contour. All five interior samples of every listed pair lie in the exact final fluted STL. The shared groove is 4 mm wide, 1.2 mm deep and has a 5 mm smoothstep fade; current pitch is 5.0073 mm. The corner-coupon and appearance scopes are recorded in cadlib/flute-evidence/README.md. This permits this specified cosmetic contour, without a 3 mm finished-wall, current deposition or load-capacity acceptance.
alternatives: Flattening or shallowing changes the selected visible profile; widening lands changes the closed field. Assess any finish change against the appearance evidence rather than selecting it from a thickness cutoff.
